# Stack and TypeScript

## Locked stack

- Next.js App Router (see `AGENTS.md` / `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using Next APIs)
- React 19 + TypeScript (`strict`)
- Tailwind CSS 4 + existing tokens/utilities in `app/globals.css`
- UI: shadcn / Radix (`components/ui`) + `lucide-react` icons + `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`
- Forms: `react-hook-form` + Zod (`zod` / `@hookform/resolvers`)
- Backend integrations already in repo: Supabase, Stripe, Resend, Packeta

Do not introduce alternate UI kits, state libraries, CSS frameworks, ORMs, or form libraries.

## TypeScript

- Write TypeScript only for app code; do not add new plain JS modules.
- Keep `strict` typing; avoid `any`. Prefer existing types in `app/types`, Zod schemas, and inferred types.
- Use path alias `@/` for imports.
- Prefer narrowing and Zod validation over type assertions.
- Reuse helpers in `helpers/` and `lib/` before creating new utilities.

## UI and copy

- Follow existing component structure (`components/sections`, `components/ui`, `components/admin`).
- Prefer Server Components; add `"use client"` only when interactivity or browser APIs require it.
- Keep user-facing copy in Slovak unless asked otherwise.
- Match existing spacing, color, and typography patterns; do not restyle unrelated UI.
- Extract a reusable component only when the same UI/logic is clearly needed in more than one place, or when it cleanly mirrors an existing pattern. Prefer extending `components/ui` or nearby section components over inventing a parallel abstraction.
